WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.757
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:16.784
Unit eleven: Rivers and Mountains. In this unit, you will compare rivers, lakes and mountains.

4
00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:18.610
River.

5
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.749
River means a long line of water that flows to the sea.

6
00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:24.852
The river is wide and brown.

7
00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:28.680
Your turn. Say: River.

8
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.091
River.

9
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:33.933
Mountain.

10
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.587
Mountain means a very high hill.

11
00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:38.271
We climbed the mountain.

12
00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.867
Your turn. Say: Mountain.

13
00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:45.452
Mountain.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.207
Lake.

15
00:00:47.907 --> 00:00:51.857
Lake means a big area of water with land all around it.

16
00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:53.704
There are boats on the lake.

17
00:00:54.404 --> 00:00:56.917
Your turn. Say: Lake.

18
00:00:59.617 --> 00:01:00.398
Lake.

19
00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:02.350
Mekong.

20
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.152
Mekong means the longest river in Southeast Asia.

21
00:01:06.452 --> 00:01:08.568
The Mekong flows through Cambodia.

22
00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.955
Your turn. Say: Mekong.

23
00:01:14.655 --> 00:01:15.482
Mekong.

24
00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:17.589
Tonle Sap.

25
00:01:18.289 --> 00:01:21.159
Tonle Sap means the biggest lake in Cambodia.

26
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:23.656
Many fish live in the Tonle Sap.

27
00:01:24.356 --> 00:01:27.357
Your turn. Say: Tonle Sap.

28
00:01:30.057 --> 00:01:31.186
Tonle Sap.

29
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:33.080
High.

30
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.116
High means a long way up from the ground.

31
00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:38.265
Phnom Aural is very high.

32
00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.733
Your turn. Say: High.

33
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:45.190
High.

34
00:01:46.183 --> 00:01:46.801
Long.

35
00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.209
Long means far from one end to the other.

36
00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:52.276
The Mekong is a long river.

37
00:01:52.976 --> 00:01:55.791
Your turn. Say: Long.

38
00:01:58.491 --> 00:01:59.260
Long.

39
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:00.996
Fish.

40
00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:05.181
Fish means an animal that lives and swims in water.

41
00:02:05.481 --> 00:02:07.458
Fishermen catch fish in the lake.

42
00:02:08.158 --> 00:02:11.065
Your turn. Say: Fish.

43
00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:14.581
Fish.

44
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:17.641
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.941 --> 00:02:23.098
Rithy, which is longer, the Mekong or the Tonle Sap River?

46
00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:25.768
The Mekong is longer.

47
00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:30.572
Right! And what is the highest mountain in Cambodia?

48
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:34.954
Phnom Aural. It is higher than Phnom Kulen.

49
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.122
Have you seen the Tonle Sap Lake?

50
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:42.313
Yes! It is bigger than any lake I know.

51
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:47.253
Grammar focus: Comparatives (long to longer).

52
00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:49.739
The Mekong is longer than our river.

53
00:02:50.039 --> 00:02:54.885
Add -er and 'than' to compare two things. For big, double the g: bigger.

54
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:59.871
Now read and listen. Water and Hills of Cambodia.

55
00:03:00.171 --> 00:03:03.552
The Mekong is a long river that flows through Cambodia.

56
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.674
The Tonle Sap is a big lake with many fish.

57
00:03:08.983 --> 00:03:12.306
In the rainy season, the lake becomes much bigger.

58
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:16.940
The highest mountain in Cambodia is Phnom Aural.

59
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.130
Rivers and mountains are beautiful, so we must keep them clean.

60
00:03:23.417 --> 00:03:26.243
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:26.543 --> 00:03:28.763
The Mekong is blank than our river.

62
00:03:29.063 --> 00:03:32.612
A, long. B, longer. C, longest.

63
00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:39.023
The answer is B: longer.

64
00:03:40.517 --> 00:03:43.015
The biggest lake in Cambodia is the blank.

65
00:03:43.315 --> 00:03:47.840
A, Tonle Sap. B, Mekong. C, Phnom Aural.

66
00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.453
The answer is A: Tonle Sap.

67
00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.507
Phnom Aural is blank than Phnom Kulen.

68
00:03:58.807 --> 00:04:02.576
A, high. B, higher. C, highly.

69
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:09.198
The answer is B: higher.

70
00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:15.135
Now it's your turn to speak. Have you ever seen a big river or mountain?

71
00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:26.454
Yes, I have seen the Mekong River. It is longer and wider than the river in my village.

72
00:04:26.754 --> 00:04:28.429
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:34.124
Great work today! You learned eight new words and comparatives (long to longer).

74
00:04:34.424 --> 00:04:39.596
Today's value is love of nature. Enjoy and protect rivers and mountains.

75
00:04:39.896 --> 00:04:42.362
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

76
00:04:42.662 --> 00:04:45.605
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

